In article <11648@s.ms.uky.edu>, aash@ms.uky.edu (aash) writes:
> There is an absolutely infuriating bug in Nethack that got
> me yesterday.  It happens when you do an inventory, and you
> have the amulet.  Segmentation fault.  But not always, and
> I'm not sure what other thing could lead to it.  I do know
> that this has happened several times on several different
> machines and installations, so it is not machine specific.

I had this happen to me enough times to get really mad and dig
through the sources. It turned out that the wizard was cursing
my previously blessed weapon. Attempts to do any inventory command
that would display the weapon would cause the segmentation fault,
because the string "a cursed blessed ..." was too long for the buffer
allocated for it. I changed the code that did curses to check for
previously blessed weapons, and had the curse simply undo the blessing
(which seems to make more sense anyways!). This seemed to do the trick.
Sorry I can't be more specific, but the NetHack sources are no longer
on my hard disk, so no context diffs are available -- try grep'ing
for a routine called "do_curse" or something similar.
